Q: join two lists of dictionaries on a single key A: <p>You can do this by creating a another dictionary and that is the way of doing in <code>O(n)</code> time</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>l_dict = {item['index']: item for item in l2}

result = [
    {**l, **l_dict[l['index']]}
    for l in l1
    if l['index'] in l_dict
]
</code></pre>

Q: NuGet VS 2012 ServicePointManager does not support proxies with the https scheme A: <p>I was facing same proxy issue but I modified nuget.config file present in the solution. I don't have admin privileges since its enterprise machine.<br />
Basically, added below line in configuration and ran dotnet restore. it worked.</p>
<pre><code>    &lt;config&gt;
        &lt;add key=&quot;http_proxy&quot; value=&quot;&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;add key=&quot;https_proxy&quot; value=&quot;&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;add key=&quot;no_proxy&quot; value=&quot;localhost&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/config&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: React native Lottie animations onAnimationFinish doesn&#39;t work on ios A: <p>Unfortunately the <code>onAnimationFinished</code> callback is not stable neither on Android nor on IOS, that's why it is better that you handle it manually, like to code snippet below:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const ANIMATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT = 5000;


function YourWrapperComponent({ handleAnimationFinish }) {
  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    let timerID: number | NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;

    function handleLottieAnimationInAndroid() {
      ref.current?.play();

      timerID = setTimeout(() =&gt; {
        handleAnimationFinish?.();
      }, ANIMATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT);
    }

    handleLottieAnimationInAndroid();
    return () =&gt; {
      if (timerID) {
        clearTimeout(timerID);
      }
    };
  }, [handleAnimationFinish]);


return (
     &lt;View style={styles.container}&gt;
      &lt;LottieView
        ref={ref}
        source={require('@/../assets/animations/lotties/splash-screen.json')}
        autoPlay={false}
        loop={false}
        resizeMode=&quot;contain&quot;
        style={{
          width: metrics.getVW(100),
          height: metrics.getVH(100),
        }}
        duration={3200}
      /&gt;
    &lt;/View&gt;
);
</code></pre>
<p>Note: You have to be cautious about the <code>ANIMATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT</code>, it may vary between the platforms, for example: it can be 5000ms for Android and 4600ms for IOS. Anyone that welling to implement my solution, have to test it well on the different platforms as well as on different devices with different capabilities.</p>
<p>Please check this <a href="https://github.com/lottie-react-native/lottie-react-native#:%7E:text=Additionally%2C%20there%20is%20an%20imperative%20API%20which%20is%20sometimes%20simpler." rel="nofollow noreferrer">link for the manual animation.</a></p>
